From 1c653d894ae354d7f45e004553bb6d5d3f8e7e95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: auricom <27022259+auricom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:43:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add RollupNodeInstanceType for single-NVMe rollup nodes

The rollup launch templates hard-coded c8gd.12xlarge and the RAID-0 disk
profiles. RollupNodeInstanceType (c8gd.12xlarge | i8g.4xlarge) now sets
the instance type of the primary, secondary and backup nodes and selects
the matching layout: i8g.4xlarge uses the single-NVMe Ansible profiles
(aws_single_nvme_ebs_logs, aws_ebs_backup_node_single_nvme) and gets a
64 GiB gp3 logs volume on /dev/sdg. The default keeps existing
deployments on c8gd.12xlarge with unchanged resolved resources.

Also point the RestoreFromVolumeInstructions output at the restore
script Ansible actually installs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
